// A range without an end can't be made into a list, so `map`, `filter` and
// the other steps give a lazy sequence for one, without `lazy`.
// expect-output: [1,4,9]
// expect-output: 12
// expect-output: [(0,5),(1,6)]
print((1..).map(fn(x) => x * x).take(3).list);
print((1..).filter(fn(x) => x % 4 == 0).skip(2).first_or(0));
print((5..).enumerate().take(2).list);
